id: pm-n912nt
title: "Transactional preview portability: canonical race fixtures and persistent invalid-path recovery"
description: "GH-1377/1378/1380 expose separate portable-boundary regressions in the semantic-preview acceptance added by pm-gh1370: race injection compares unresolved aliases to canonical paths, a search cursor fixture hashes an unresolved Windows root, and ENOENT below a regular file is incorrectly treated as disappearance on Windows. Repair concrete causes and make these contracts mandatory before merge without weakening assertions or platform coverage."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: context-management,github-intake,portability,regression
created_at: "2026-10-03T20:11:29.225Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-03T22:56:12.977Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#c34534ca90095a05f3a48f57"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Canonical settings race injection executes on physical and aliased roots across macOS Windows and Linux;Persistent invalid intermediate path errors retain native diagnostics while vanished entries retain retryable conflicts;Search cursor continuation fixture hashes the actual resolved tracker;Required platform checks exercise settings search and snapshot cases with unchanged assertions;Full-source coverage remains 100/100/100/100
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "Canonical physical/aliased race fixtures and resolved cursor scopes pass on native Windows, macOS and Linux. Persistent invalid-path diagnostics are preserved, disappearing entries retry safely, and every source coverage metric remains exactly 100 percent."
actual_result: "Pre-fix boundary controls reproduced cursor and persistent-path failures. Focused real-filesystem, SDK and linked tests now pass. Native focused checks pass; complete hosted validation identified remaining registry-fixture ordering and missing planning metadata, which are being corrected without weakening gates."
